The repository contains three Python packages, all under the same licence:

  packages/precedent  (distribution name: precedent-cli)
      The CLI and the verified self-modification loop: correction miner, rule
      DSL, temporal birth gate, docket, hook suite, snapshot/undo, examiner,
      nightly improver, audit report.

  packages/receipts   (distribution name: receipts)
      Read-only load receipts, change feed and activation funnel for Claude
      Code learned state.

  packages/acceptor   (distribution name: acceptor)
      The anytime-valid acceptance core: paired e-process gates, CTHS spend
      schedules, protected-task floors, hard constraints and the sha256
      hash-chained certificate ledger.

Third-party dependencies
------------------------
The runtime is the Python standard library.  There are exactly two optional
extras, and both degrade gracefully when absent:

  precedent-cli[zh]  ->  jieba (MIT License, https://github.com/fxsjy/jieba)
                         Chinese word segmentation for the correction miner's
                         topic grouping.  Without it the tokeniser falls back
                         to character bigrams and every report says which one
                         ran.

  *[test]            ->  pytest (MIT License, https://pytest.org)

Precedent invokes the `claude` command-line tool as an external subprocess for
the three optional commands that cost money (`compile --llm`, `improve`,
`examine`).  That binary is not distributed with, bundled into, or a dependency
of this project.

Research corpus
---------------
`research/` contains the raw data behind the design (a 521-item landscape
index, 96 deep reads, six narratives, four gap analyses, six independent
designs and thirteen reviews).  It quotes and summarises third-party papers,
repositories and issue trackers for the purpose of analysis and citation; the
summaries are this project's work, the underlying works belong to their
authors, and every claim carries a URL back to its source.  See
research/README.md.

